{"messages":[{"content":"","role":"system","sections":{"cwd":"<cwd>\n[path:0364f2f649489d76062c]\n</cwd>","docs":"<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: [path:d82ac5af04c0100a85ce]\n- Additional docs: [path:bb144c96a9d247c07d6f]\n- Examples: [path:0326e6e587bc39169964] (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>","preamble":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.","rules":"<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Use codemode to batch independent tool calls (Promise.allSettled), chain them, or filter large output, instead of many separate calls.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>","tools":"<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n- codemode: Run JavaScript that calls other tools\n- tool_search: Search for tools that are not loaded yet and load the matches\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>"},"timestamp":1795610206406,"toolsAdded":[{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"For Notion introductions, summaries, comparisons or inspection, copy a supplied Skill/resource ref into path. This reads content without loading Requires or activating its workflow. If the task already calls for applying a chosen Skill, call notion_use directly; it loads the root and Requires without a preliminary main read. For a requested latest-version inspection, use refresh:true with the supplied main Skill ref; the current task keeps its previous selection. To adopt the latest instructions, call notion_use with refresh:true directly. Reuse a complete successful read. Notion reads do not write to the remote library. Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete. Alternatively, paths reads fixed resources of one owner and snapshot together; choose path or paths. Batch reads exclude offset/limit and the main entrypoint.\n\nCodemode: `tools.read(args)` resolves to a value; `await describeTool(\"read\")` shows its type.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"budget":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"For a user-requested bounded wait on a resource paths batch only. timeBudgetMs covers the complete operation, including lookup and acquisition; default 30000, maximum 120000. File and byte limits stay unchanged. No automatic retry.","properties":{"timeBudgetMs":{"maximum":120000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["timeBudgetMs"],"type":"object"},"from":{"description":"For an authored relative file link, copy the fixed sr:S/sr:R or canonical skill:// ref of the actual file containing that link. Put the original relative link in path. Nested documents use their own resource ref, not the main Skill ref. Source-backed cross-Skill links resolve through the shared Source mapping; targets keep their own versions. Excludes paths batches and refresh:true.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read","type":"number"},"offset":{"description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)","type":"number"},"path":{"description":"Local file path (relative or absolute), an issued skill:// or sr: ref, or a supplied Notion Skill page URL. Notion main reads inspect without adopting task instructions. Copy refs verbatim; never guess filesystem paths.","type":"string"},"paths":{"description":"Copy complete resource refs verbatim from the selected Skill snapshot's resource directory. Every ref must identify a file in the same owner and snapshot. Reads all selected files in one operation without preparing the main body.","items":{"pattern":"^(?:sr:R[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}|skill:\\/\\/.+)$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"refresh":{"description":"Use only for a user-requested current-version inspection; a successful complete read needs no follow-up refresh. Keeps the active selection unchanged. Only for a supplied Notion Skill ref in path; fixed resources and local files keep their versions.","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\n\nCodemode: `tools.bash(args)` resolves to `{ output, truncated, full_output_path?, exit_code, wall_time_seconds }`.","name":"bash","parameters":{"properties":{"command":{"description":"Shell command to execute","type":"string"},"timeout":{"description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)","type":"number"}},"required":["command"],"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\n\nCodemode: `tools.edit(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"edit","parameters":{"properties":{"edits":{"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.","items":{"properties":{"newText":{"description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit.","type":"string"},"oldText":{"description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.","type":"string"}},"required":["oldText","newText"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","edits"],"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\n\nCodemode: `tools.write(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"write","parameters":{"properties":{"content":{"description":"Content to write to the file","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"],"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"type":"grammar","variants":{"openai_lark":"\nstart: options_source | plain_source\noptions_source: OPTIONS_LINE NEWLINE SOURCE\nplain_source: SOURCE\n\nOPTIONS_LINE: /[ \\t]*\\/\\/ @options:[^\\r\\n]*/\nNEWLINE: /\\r?\\n/\nSOURCE: /[\\s\\S]+/\n"}},"description":"Run JavaScript that calls other tools. The input is raw JavaScript (not JSON, no code fence), run as an async function body in a QuickJS sandbox: top-level `await` and `return` work. No Node, file system, network, or timers.\n- `await tools.<name>({ ...args })` resolves to a string, or an object if the tool's declaration says so, and rejects with an Error on failure. A tool whose declaration returns an object resolves on failure too when it returned that object; check its fields. Calls still running when the script ends are cancelled.\n- Optional first line: `// @options: {\"max_output_tokens\": 10000, \"timeout_ms\": 60000}`\n\nGlobals:\n- `text(value)`, `image(dataUrlOrImageBlock)`, `console.log(...)`, and top-level `return` add output; `exit()` ends the script. With several text items, each starts with a `==> text N/M <==` line, and `console` lines follow the other output in one `<console_output>` block. `image()` also saves the image to a temp file and the result names its path.\n- `store(key, value)` and `load(key)` keep JSON values across codemode calls.\n- `ALL_TOOLS`, `await searchTools(query, { limit?, namespace? })`, `await describeTool(name)`, `await describeNamespace(name)`: find unlisted tools, such as MCP tools.","name":"codemode","parameters":{"properties":{"code":{"description":"Raw JavaScript source.","type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"type":"object"}},{"description":"# Tool discovery\n\nSearches over deferred tool metadata with BM25 and exposes matching tools for the next model call.\n\nSome of the tools, such as tools of MCP servers, may not have been provided to you upfront, and you should use this tool (`tool_search`) to search for the required tools. For MCP tool discovery, always use `tool_search`.","name":"tool_search","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of tools to return. Defaults to 8.","type":"number"},"query":{"description":"Search query for deferred tools.","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},{"description":"Search the authorized Skill metadata directory, including items outside the default View. Returns Skill refs for read or notion_use; it does not load instructions or activate workflows. For named Notion Skill existence or availability questions, set query to the name and refresh:true, even when already listed or previously absent. Answer existence and stated-purpose questions from metadata; read or use the Skill only when the user asks to inspect or apply its instructions. Also refresh after writes or to request the latest directory; selected Skill versions stay fixed. Report matching availability. Only fresh online results with exhaustive coverage and no failures establish that no available match was found in the searched scope; stale, offline, failed or partial results cannot establish current absence.\n\nCodemode: `tools.notion_list(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"notion_list","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Copy next_cursor to continue the same query and metadata publication; restart after refresh.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum metadata entries, default 20.","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"A short name or description keyword; empty lists the directory.","type":"string"},"refresh":{"description":"Refresh metadata for source, or all configured Notion sources when source is omitted. Keeps task pins; configured offline sources remain offline. Cannot combine with cursor.","type":"boolean"},"source":{"description":"Optional configured source ID to disambiguate directories.","type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"description":"Load task roots directly to apply their instructions; no preliminary read is needed. Requires load automatically: do not add them as independent roots unless independently requested. To introduce, summarize or inspect a Skill, use read instead. Copy a supplied ref, or pass task roots together. Use refresh:true only for a requested update; the supplied current or fixed main ref locates the same owner's latest version. Refresh roots with conflicting shared Requires together. Members remain candidates. Loading does not authorize executing a workflow. Notion consumption does not write to Notion.","name":"notion_use","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":64,"minItems":1,"type":"array"}],"description":"Supplied sr:C/sr:S or skill://<name-or-id>/<main> refs, or exact Notion Skill page URLs for task roots. Requires are included automatically. Prefer returned canonical refs for later actions."},"refresh":{"description":"Explicitly adopt current versions for only these roots after a complete successful load. Existing Requires-only nodes cannot become independent roots through refresh; explicitly use them without refresh first. Accepts the supplied sr:C/sr:S or main ref unchanged, for example {ref:[REF_A,REF_B],refresh:true} for shared roots. Failure keeps the previous selection.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}}]},{"content":[{"text":"<ntn-skills-view-catalog>\nDefault Notion candidates. Inspect with read; use a Skill through the available use tool. Discover other authorized entries with notion_list. Previously loaded bodies keep their selected versions.\n<view source=\"notion\" id=\"[id:c3134f60c2e4e5ed004b]\" database=\"[id:44466957e41791517591]\" origin=\"first\" count=\"16\" partial=\"false\">Default view</view>\n<catalog-cards>\n<group kind=\"skill\" source=\"notion\">\n<card name=\"[identity:48a84c1ae8e247db6003]\" location=\"sr:CQrSJsfyy12FAfoWy6eLr4g\">松涛51配送方式报价规则</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:047f7cf18eb447e105c3]\" location=\"sr:CTFGW_iCwuxQEXA8P7Ixn1w\">松涛53外发报表个人信息处理</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:09623e3c729fffd6ee93]\" location=\"sr:CFtDrUdWw8wggpSDEFkEhWA\">松涛53交易金额对账</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:06f337cb608e803a0f47]\" location=\"sr:CGm3nhoCrKjqsJ06jPzhD9g\">松涛39包裹运输路由规则</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:3273900c18323a4eafbe]\" location=\"sr:CvTIjCEqQSRqrQUfR1DfeSg\">松涛12发票含税金额计算</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:6f3f39988438e796905f]\" location=\"sr:Cp4TV2VGKqYUt65gzduK12w\">松涛12按行计算税额</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:2afd5579b9b4f4670b87]\" location=\"sr:CUMkZ_exi9SozAFaYit_8ow\">松涛73退货审批政策</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:708a7d053c4b7bbb836e]\" location=\"sr:CQemOEBeSh30ZqvH1IsQ1JQ\">松涛92包裹运输路由规则</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:a74f28a9b2575cb8da08]\" location=\"sr:CBv1l-_oNf4fWWW365IZ7pQ\">松涛98区域资助资格政策</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:a8b0d1818cc535c1b759]\" location=\"sr:CnKek75FHOEOU8Hm_CkW1kg\">松涛44仓库批次清单整理</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:f39cfadb581363d708da]\" location=\"sr:CEQgY3Vtrhu5ZSB_fWdsPug\">仅处理会议座位编排</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:6a14c1e90ffb2f4a4bdb]\" location=\"sr:CTtc5Lm9XaJ4MgNyyqEUG0A\">仅处理图书馆借阅标签</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:9c8fd14c6ea6340dc3a1]\" location=\"sr:Cmg3nBpYrmgprLYTQztmd_w\">仅处理摄影文件命名</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:f3878d3b1b9951c080eb]\" location=\"sr:CJVWBgDqBC9pu7QV-590e0g\">仅处理运动器材盘点</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:9b1480db222797690445]\" location=\"sr:C3sQkBwvDSNlVe8xU5ZLvTg\">仅处理菜园采收日志</card>\n<card name=\"[identity:8d9064601c6ab3c0c0d6]\" location=\"sr:CSjafP3otHX-8OTd6K8IP_Q\">松涛40库存补货规则</card>\n</group>\n</catalog-cards>\n</ntn-skills-view-catalog>","type":"text"}],"role":"user","timestamp":0},{"content":[{"text":"请把 input/manifest.csv 整理成 松涛44 仓库使用的标准批次清单，保留 id、depot、count 并附导入格式标识 format_marker_hex，保存到 output/manifest-clean.json。","type":"text"}],"role":"user","timestamp":1795610206406},{"content":[{"text":"<ntn-skills-guidance>\nLocal @Skills keep native availability. Honor explicit source and prior choice. Equal same-name local/Notion fits: clarify; storage gives no priority. Clear fit/equivalent copies: no question. Editor flags grant no permissions.\nReuse complete content. Inspection never activates. Loading authorizes no commands/writes/delegation.\nnotion_list: beyond the default View. Named Notion existence/availability: query:name,refresh:true; metadata only, keeping pins. Also after writes. Check freshness/coverage; failed/partial/offline is not absence.\nread(path) inspects. refresh:true checks latest main; pins fixed. Notion page URLs: exact owners. Keep owner/snapshot; never edit sr: handles. paths: same snapshot.\nUse/follow even read-only: notion_use(ref) applies with Requires; refresh:true adopts latest on request, conflicting roots together. Members: candidates. Outside Code mode.\nMaintenance: read ntn-skills-maintain's exact ref in task's source/library; absent/pending: notion_list there. To apply: notion_use(ref), same ref + Requires. Edited item: inspect only. Builtins: explicit offline/bootstrap only.\nOnly explicit offline/bootstrap/installed-package help: read(\"[path:bb3f132305e9b1be7023]\"), paired package. No fallback for pending/failed Notion; never search other installations.\nCLI management: tool_search for notion_ctl, then its cli_source. Choose explicitly from [\"notion\"]; use returned command/scope, never a global CLI. No execution or authorization.\n</ntn-skills-guidance>","type":"text"}],"role":"user","timestamp":1795610206407},{"api":"openai-responses","content":[{"thinking":"Organizing input/manifest.csv into a standard batch manifest for 松涛44 warehouse. Retaining id, depot, and count. Adding format_marker_hex. Saving to output/manifest-clean.json.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"[REDACTED]\",\"id\":\"rs_205a7feb-5011-4b80-82c6-9b7e6458ef2b\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"Organizing input/manifest.csv into a standard batch manifest for 松涛44 warehouse. Retaining id, depot, and count. Adding format_marker_hex. Saving to output/manifest-clean.json.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}","type":"thinking"},{"text":"先加载松涛44 仓库批次清单整理技能，再按它的规则处理 `input/manifest.csv`。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_205a7feb-5011-4b80-82c6-9b7e6458ef2b\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}","type":"text"},{"arguments":{"ref":"sr:CnKek75FHOEOU8Hm_CkW1kg"},"id":"call-[id:176ff0fe0441f79ee08e]-0|fc_205a7feb-5011-4b80-82c6-9b7e6458ef2b_0","name":"notion_use","type":"toolCall"}],"durationMs":5144,"model":"auto/grok-4.6","provider":"[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]","rawStopReason":"completed","responseId":"[id:06a8e51d99be6790d640]","role":"assistant","stopReason":"toolUse","thinkingLevel":"medium","timestamp":1795610206469,"usage":{"cacheRead":128,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":{"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"input":0,"output":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"input":4820,"output":161,"reasoning":110,"totalTokens":5109}},{"content":[{"text":"{\"ok\":true,\"status\":\"ready\",\"purpose\":\"use\",\"roots\":[\"sr:SSfconfGB-20nMuDKjabqHQ\"],\"records\":[{\"name\":\"[identity:a8b0d1818cc535c1b759]\",\"kind\":\"skill\",\"ref\":\"sr:SSfconfGB-20nMuDKjabqHQ\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: [identity:a8b0d1818cc535c1b759]\\ndescription: \\\"松涛44仓库批次清单整理\\\"\\n---\\n\\n\\n# 松涛44仓库批次清单整理\\n\\n清单是简单三列 CSV，没有逗号转义。去掉单元格首尾空格，把 depot 按 assets/depots.json 转为代码，count 转为整数。scripts/normalize.mjs 可执行同样转换，输入和输出路径分别为两个参数。可执行脚本，也可按相同规则处理。每行必须附上 assets/format-marker.bin 字节的小写十六进制值作为 format\\\\_marker\\\\_hex。输出 id、depot、count、format\\\\_marker\\\\_hex。\\n\\n本材料为可公开复现的合成业务资料，许可 CC0-1.0。\\n\\n金额一律使用整数分；若有舍入，按文中规则执行。\",\"directory\":{\